2026-06-26 14:13:32,551 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-26 14:13:32,551 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: We already have several relevant security controls in place. For GDPR compliance, our data hosting is supported by OuraneCloud, which holds the SecNumCloud qualification, ensuring sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU. We also utilize encryption in transit via TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, with key management based on EU-based infrastructure. Additionally, we implement pseudonymisation where applicable.

To ensure explainability and auditability of AI outputs, our product Atelier is designed to provide grounded and traceable figures or factual statements, with retrieval trace and figure source linking capabilities. This aligns with the requirement for explainability and auditable outputs.

We also maintain strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, preventing any cross-client circulation of data, which supports separation of duties and respect for auditor's independence. Our role-based access control (RBAC) and audit logging further ensure that all system activities are logged and can be reviewed, supporting compliance with anti-money laundering obligations.

Moreover, our incident response plan includes detection, notification, and remediation procedures, including a 72-hour GDPR breach-notification workflow, ensuring timely action in case of any data breaches. Our secure software development life cycle (SDLC) incorporates code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external provider of equivalent CREST level, which helps in identifying and remediating vulnerabilities.

Lastly, we are ISO 27001 certified since 2023, with a scope covering Development, delivery, and operations, and also hold the ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management. These certifications demonstrate our commitment to information security and privacy management, aligning with the requirements for GDPR compliance and respect for professional secrecy and confidentiality.

Therefore, based on our existing context, we have a solid foundation of security controls that address the regulatory requirements mentioned in the tender, including GDPR compliance, explainability and auditability of AI outputs, separation of duties, auditor's independence, and anti-money laundering obligations.
